### Requirement Candidate Format

Every derivation path produces candidates in the same top-layer format. Only the traceability metadata differs.

```markdown
#### RC-{SCOPE}-NNN: {Title}

- **Type:** {Business rule | Functional | Non-functional}
- **Statement:** {What must be true — domain language, testable, forward-facing}
- **Acceptance criteria:**
  - {Testable assertion using observable behavior and domain vocabulary}
  - {Another testable assertion}
- **{Traceability section — varies by path}**
- **Confidence:** {High | Medium | Low — with rationale if not High}
```

**Format consistency requirement:** The top-layer requirement (statement + acceptance criteria) is structurally identical regardless of derivation path. A reader should not be able to tell whether a requirement came from regulation, enterprise standards, or source code without looking at the traceability section.
